decisionsSection:
**The owner, 2026-11-04:** «Fa tor ce ai zis și mai devreme» — the race's plan: «Locurile libere le dau doar eu» ticked, a waiting list of 20, and every place given by hand from it («Trimite-i oferta», «Oferă-i un loc acum»).

**Why.** Round five of the review of feat/registration-control named the pages a person reads once they are in the line that still promised a freed place reaches them by itself — «Dacă se eliberează un loc, îți scriem…» — while the tick, or «Nu», leaves every place to the organizers. With the tick on the race, everybody the site sends to the line would read a promise nobody keeps.

**Decision.** One rule, the allocator's own (`domain/waitlist.ts#offersOnItsOwn`: «Locurile din lista de așteptare se alocă automat» on «Da» and «Locurile libere le dau doar eu» off), read where each page already stands, never a second copy. While it is false, each place says the organizers give the places one at a time and write when they can give one; with «Da» and the tick off, today's words:

- **the address confirmed onto the line** (`/registrations/confirm/[token]?done=waitlist`) and the list of the address's people under it — `Registrations.confirm.doneWaitlistByHand`, `confirm.nextWaitlistedByHand`;
- **the declaration signed onto the line** — the page's three lines of what comes next (`declare.nextWaitlistedByHand`: the promise, and «organizatorii pot da locul altcuiva» past an offer's deadline in place of «locul merge mai departe», as `WAITLIST_SPOT_OFFER` says it) — and **a family's last screen** there, its waiting person's line (`declare.family.what.waitlistedByHand`);
- **another person on the address entered onto the line** (`/registrations/family/[token]?done=waitlist`, `family.doneWaitlistByHand`);
- **a spent link of somebody waiting** («Ești pe lista de așteptare», `spent.waitHelpByHand`);
- **the steps' «Dacă nu mai sunt locuri»** on the register page, the event page and the editor's preview (`Registration.steps.waitingList.bodyByHand`), without «în ordinea înscrierii» too: the organizers choose (§627);
- **the public list's legend** for «Pe lista de așteptare» (`Event.startList.legend.waitlistedByHand`: «Locurile le dau organizatorii, pe rând: cine primește o ofertă pe email are {offer} ca să semneze declarația.»);
- **«Ce îi spui»** on a waiting registration (`Admin.registrations.tell.waitlistedByHand`), word for word the `WAITLIST_JOINED` email's own sentence for the same event («Locurile le dau organizatorii, pe rând: îți scriem când îți putem da un loc.»), a unit test keeping the pair equal as it keeps «Te vom anunța dacă se eliberează un loc.».

Where each reads the rule: the pages after a press ask the event the spent link names (`token-actions.ts#spentLinkOffersByItself` over `repository.ts#offersWaitlistAutomatically`, the reader the emails use when they are rendered); a family's last screen asks the event its pass names; a spent link's page reads it in `readSpentRegistrationLink`'s own transaction (`byItself`, for a person waiting, absent otherwise); the steps and the legend read the public row through `registration-cta.ts#offersByItself`, places counted (a full event's step, a waiting row's legend); «Ce îi spui» reads `repository.ts#lineOffersOnItsOwn`, the column it already read for the line's order. Each reads it only when somebody on the page waits. A row read without the settings is «Da», the column's default. `RegistrationSteps` requires `byItself` of every caller, and `FamilySigningSteps` of its last screen, so no page can forget it.

**`WAITLIST_OFFER_EXPIRED` is left as it was.** Its «… te vom anunța dacă se mai eliberează un loc» is never sent: nothing queues it (§331, `domain/never-queued.ts`, held by a test), and an offer's lapse moves the row to `EXPIRED`, not back to the line (`AGENTS.md` §10.5), so its «Rămâi pe lista de așteptare» is untrue whatever the settings. Rewording its last clause would polish a message nobody receives and leave it wrong; sending it again is a decision about a lapsed offer, not a wording. A comment beside the template says so.

**Refused.** A second statement of the rule for the pages — every page reads `offersOnItsOwn` through one of its existing forms, so none can drift from the allocator's gate. Counting the event's places to say «complet» or not, as `WAITLIST_JOINED` does (`waitlistByHand`): these pages promise nothing about fullness, only who gives a place. Rewording `confirm.waitlistFull` and `confirm.noWaitlist` («dacă se eliberează un loc…, redeschide-l»): advice to press the link again, not a notice promised.
